From: FoAKTEE <hw609@cantab.ac.uk>
Date: Fri, 25 Sep 2026 12:02:14 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 09/16] feat(m3-march): adopt the BlackLightPlus march control,
 termination and sample set

- change: integrate_geodesic_state (STEP_BBH): RK4 with h = min_A (r_A - r_h,A) / C; captured when the horizon distance is below horizon_eps, non-finite, or the normal-frame energy |k^t|/sqrt(-g^tt) exceeds capture_redshift; escaped when R > escape and increasing; nmax steps; theta-turn cut removed
- change: the terminal state and its end class (1/2 hole, 3 escape, 4 budget, 5 non-finite) are stored after the last lightpath entry
- finding: upstream RT pairs state n with the step into it (dl[n-1]) and skips state 0; BlackLightPlus pairs every state with the step taken from it (reverse_march.jl StoredPath). Under STEP_BBH both transfer loops use the BlackLightPlus pairing; the polarized loop transports f over the step between n and n-1 with the stored k, and k is no longer re-nulled [SOLID]
- result: R04 legs (kerr, s455, s122; 1050 rays each): termination class identical on 100% of rays, sample counts equal on every ray, RK4 order 4.0 (C 40-80) against a Vern7 reference [SOLID]
- verify: BlackLightPlus results/blp/raptor/tools/r04_rays.jl
